            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0877" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/440: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia (Mitchell) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-21T16:00:00-00:44">December 21, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 22—2:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. Called on Barclay at 2:30. After
                    reciting to him the contents of the Department’s 76, December 19, 6 p.m.,
                        Barclay and Grimes, who was also present, stated that they
                    could not act on a verbal representation but would be glad to give it
                    consideration if such information were submitted in the form of an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mitchell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
